{"nodes": [{"id": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_covid_diagnosis", "label": "Why the COVID Single-Disease Encoder Has No Skill", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/Report_Covid.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Diagnosis complete, two candidate fixes tested end to end and one rejected; no bundle rebuilt and no canonical record overwritten."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_omicron_structural_break", "label": "Omicron as a 6x Structural Break", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/Report_Covid.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "5.1 million national weekly cases at week 102, the largest value in a 164-week series, sitting at 62% through it; the panel breaks the stationarity assumption the whole protocol rests on in five separate places at once."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_no_signal_long_horizon", "label": "No Linear Predictability at h10 and h15 on the Test Fold", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/Report_Covid.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Test-fold lag-10 autocorrelation is +0.015 and lag-15 is -0.048 while train carries +0.350 and +0.282, so no model can beat a constant there; this is a property of the data provable without running anything and is the single largest term in the deficit."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_val_fold_omicron_peak", "label": "The Validation Fold Is the Omicron Peak", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/Report_Covid.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Val runs at 2.83x both other folds and requires extrapolation, and two mechanisms key off it: early stopping selects on it and the bias correction is fitted on it, then applied to a test fold at a sixth of the scale."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_covid_val_probe", "label": "covid_val_probe.py (Test 1: Model Selection)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/Report_Covid.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three arms, one variable each, with arm A reproducing the on-disk records seed-for-seed as a harness self-check; cleaning the selection fold recovers 13-49%, but the excision rule peeks at test to design the protocol so it cannot ship."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_covid_split_probe", "label": "covid_split_probe.py (Test 2: A Better Split)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/Report_Covid.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Moves Omicron into train and excludes no data; rejected because the model-over-best-floor ratio is worse at three of four horizons and seed sd triples to 29-38%, which alone disqualifies it for a reported number."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_omicron_no_good_home", "label": "Omicron Has No Good Home", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/Report_Covid.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In val, selection and the bias correction target a regime absent from test; in train, the model learns 5M-scale excursions and emits them on a flat tail; in test, it is an unprecedented 3.8x event to extrapolate. The series is structurally front-loaded, so every chronological split faces the same fork."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_covid_as_transfer_source", "label": "COVID Survives as a Transfer Source, Not a Target", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/Report_Covid.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The covid-to-influenza direction rests on the influenza ceiling, which beats every floor, so it remains publishable; the influenza-to-covid direction is the uninterpretable half, and the blocker as written should be re-scoped by horizon because at h10/h15 no model can clear it."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_deaths_column_hypothesis", "label": "Untested Option: Use the Deaths Column", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/Report_Covid.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Already in the source file, so it needs no new acquisition and keeps the identical graph and node set; Omicron was enormous in cases and far smaller in deaths, so the 6x break may largely disappear. A hypothesis, not a result."}, {"id": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_encoder_mc_bias_correction", "label": "encoder_mc Bias Correction", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/outcomes/Report_Covid.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fitted on the validation fold, so on the shipped split it makes COVID worse at every horizon by 8.8 to 47.3 per cent; with the selection fold cleaned it becomes the better arm, so one change repaired two mechanisms that read the same fold."}], "edges": [{"source": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_covid_diagnosis", "target": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_omicron_structural_break", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/outcomes/Report_Covid.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_covid_diagnosis", "target": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_no_signal_long_horizon", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/outcomes/Report_Covid.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_covid_diagnosis", "target": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_val_fold_omicron_peak", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/outcomes/Report_Covid.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_covid_diagnosis", "target": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_covid_val_probe", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/outcomes/Report_Covid.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_covid_diagnosis", "target": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_covid_split_probe", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/outcomes/Report_Covid.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_covid_diagnosis", "target": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_omicron_no_good_home", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/outcomes/Report_Covid.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_covid_diagnosis", "target": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_covid_as_transfer_source", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/outcomes/Report_Covid.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_covid_diagnosis", "target": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_deaths_column_hypothesis", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/outcomes/Report_Covid.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_covid_diagnosis", "target": "progress_outcomes_report_covid_encoder_mc_bias_correction", "relation": "refe